## Implementation Details

The project correctly follows Vercel's recommended setup for Next.js App Router:
1. Analytics component imported from the correct package (`@vercel/analytics/next`)
2. Component placed in root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
3. Positioned inside the `<body>` tag after the main content
4. No additional configuration needed - Analytics will automatically track page views

## Notes

- The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices
- The Analytics component is a client component that automatically handles tracking
- No environment variables are required for basic analytics functionality
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard when deployed

## Conclusion

No code changes were required. The Vercel Web Analytics package is already properly installed and configured according to best practices for Next.js App Router projects.
